# Batch files MUST be checked out with CRLF endings.
# cmd.exe parses .bat/.cmd files by seeking through a byte-offset table that assumes
# every newline is 2 bytes (CRLF). With LF-only endings that table drifts and cmd
# starts executing garbage — commands lose leading characters, e.g.
#   setlocal -> tlocal,  cd /d -> /d,  echo -> cho
# followed by "is not recognized as an internal or external command" errors.
# Any editor or script that rewrites these files with LF-only breaks them, so pin the
# endings here rather than relying on the local core.autocrlf setting.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
